WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.663 --> 00:00:03.800
If I didn't go about teaching my children
tradition

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.303
and culture, it would be a whole gap
and we might not be able to give back.

00:00:07.704 --> 00:00:10.373
Then my family would be lost in tradition
and culture.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:17.347
That little spot back here,
just there, Beaver Dam blocking it

00:00:17.347 --> 00:00:20.683
but there's enough water flowing over it
to where we can jump it.

00:00:29.392 --> 00:00:33.096
[inaudible] Can we do that again?

00:00:33.896 --> 00:00:35.698
No, hell no.

00:00:35.898 --> 00:00:38.835
This boat that I got last year,
I was able to sell

00:00:38.835 --> 00:00:42.772
a bunch of mammoth ivory,
buy a nice big 150 motor,

00:00:42.772 --> 00:00:46.509
and it's got a jet on there. I’m
able to drive in some pretty skinny water.

00:00:46.576 --> 00:00:50.446
This boat is especially designed
for smaller numbers up here in Allakaket

00:00:53.216 --> 00:00:54.851
Oh, he's hunting just like us.

00:00:59.622 --> 00:01:01.290
Oh a little calf.

00:01:02.659 --> 00:01:03.993
Two Calves!

00:01:09.632 --> 00:01:11.834
Future generations food right there.

00:01:12.068 --> 00:01:12.702
Now, someday

00:01:12.702 --> 00:01:16.539
my kids might be hunting those calves
when they're nice, big, strong bulls.

00:01:17.573 --> 00:01:19.008
All right,

00:01:19.509 --> 00:01:23.780
Wow! We don't shoot swans when they're
paired up like that, they mate for life.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.048
You kill one of them.

00:01:25.048 --> 00:01:28.217
That other one is just going to fly around

00:01:28.217 --> 00:01:30.053
and quit eating
and just die of a broken heart.

00:01:30.053 --> 00:01:31.888
That's a happily married couple.

00:01:31.888 --> 00:01:33.556
I don't want to jump in between that.

00:01:38.995 --> 00:01:41.831
I think we've been out for at least
24 hours.

00:01:41.864 --> 00:01:43.199
I'm not totally sure.

00:01:43.199 --> 00:01:45.668
Hard to tell
when the sun doesn't really go down.

00:01:46.035 --> 00:01:47.937
We're just going to keep on trying.

00:01:47.937 --> 00:01:50.339
It'll open up wider here pretty quick.

00:02:03.886 --> 00:02:04.620
Uh oh.

00:02:08.891 --> 00:02:12.428
We really got to get up some speed
to get over this next dam.

00:02:16.332 --> 00:02:19.335
I don’t know about this.

00:02:50.066 --> 00:02:52.869
Well, trying to rip some of the sticks
out of this beaver dam.

00:02:54.504 --> 00:02:56.773
Having the kids out in the boat,
it is a safety hazard.

00:02:56.773 --> 00:03:00.209
This is springtime,
the rivers are just right above freezing.

00:03:00.243 --> 00:03:02.745
You've got a lot of water
and they get a lot of water

00:03:02.745 --> 00:03:05.815
and they get heavy
and they start flowing really fast.

00:03:19.996 --> 00:03:23.933
And if we can get some speed,
we can make it through it,

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.536
I’m sure.

00:03:43.119 --> 00:03:44.654
Whoa!

00:03:44.654 --> 00:03:47.256
[inaudible]

00:03:47.356 --> 00:03:48.658
That was pretty wild.

00:03:48.925 --> 00:03:51.594
We made it. Woo!

00:03:56.199 --> 00:03:58.701
Hard times don't last forever.

00:03:58.701 --> 00:04:00.403
Strong people do though.

00:04:05.074 --> 00:04:06.075
See him?

00:04:06.509 --> 00:04:07.510
Yea.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:08.344
Go ahead, Terry.

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:22.491
Good shot.

00:04:22.491 --> 00:04:23.459
Thanks.

00:04:23.993 --> 00:04:26.295
Canvas back!

00:04:26.295 --> 00:04:28.130
Oh!

00:04:28.798 --> 00:04:30.900
We’re 300 miles away from the ocean.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.236
We get to eat something from the ocean.

00:04:33.736 --> 00:04:34.937
It's pretty special.

